  "description": "Radicchio is a perfect example that grilling can make just about anything better. The sharp bitterness usually wreaks havoc on my taste buds, but once grilled, I found it very pleasing. It came together in a salad that was a sea of textures and tastes: grilled knob onions, lettuce, and a sherry-mustard vinaigrette.",
